        <qualifiedname>llvm::X86CallLowering::lowerFormalArguments</qualifiedname>
        <reimplements refid="classllvm_1_1_call_lowering_1a58307def319bb185729ec87853b193e9">lowerFormalArguments</reimplements>
        <param>
          <type><ref refid="classllvm_1_1_machine_i_r_builder" kindref="compound">MachineIRBuilder</ref> &amp;</type>
          <declname>MIRBuilder</declname>
        </param>
        <param>
          <type><ref refid="_a_arch64_promote_constant_8cpp_1a90f8350fecae261c25be85d38b451bff" kindref="member">const</ref> <ref refid="classllvm_1_1_function" kindref="compound">Function</ref> &amp;</type>
          <declname>F</declname>
        </param>
        <param>
          <type><ref refid="classllvm_1_1_array_ref" kindref="compound">ArrayRef</ref>&lt; <ref refid="classllvm_1_1_array_ref" kindref="compound">ArrayRef</ref>&lt; <ref refid="classllvm_1_1_register" kindref="compound">Register</ref> &gt; &gt;</type>
          <declname>VRegs</declname>
        </param>
        <param>
          <type><ref refid="classllvm_1_1_function_lowering_info" kindref="compound">FunctionLoweringInfo</ref> &amp;</type>
          <declname>FLI</declname>
        </param>
        <briefdescription>
<para>This hook must be implemented to lower the incoming (formal) arguments, described by <computeroutput>VRegs</computeroutput>, for GlobalISel. </para>
        </briefdescription>
        <detaileddescription>
<para>Each argument must end up in the related virtual registers described by <computeroutput>VRegs</computeroutput>. In other words, the first argument should end up in <computeroutput>VRegs</computeroutput>[0], the second in <computeroutput>VRegs</computeroutput>[1], and so on. For each argument, there will be one register for each non-aggregate type, as returned by <computeroutput>computeValueLLTs</computeroutput>. <computeroutput>MIRBuilder</computeroutput> is set to the proper insertion for the argument lowering. <computeroutput>FLI</computeroutput> is required for sret demotion.</para>
<para><simplesect kind="return"><para>True if the lowering succeeded, false otherwise. </para>
</simplesect>
</para>
        </detaileddescription>
